Discover ING Hubs Romania
ING Hubs Romania offers 130 services in software development, data management, non-financial risk & compliance, audit, and retail operations to 24 ING units worldwide, with the help ofover 2000 high-performing engineers, risk, and operations professionals.
We started out in 2015 as ING’s software development hub, then steadily expanded our range to include more services and competencies. Now we provide borderless services with bank-wide capabilities andoperate from two locations: Bucharest and Cluj-Napoca.
Our tech capabilities remain the core of our business, with more than 1800 colleagues active in Data and Analytics Tech, Tech Foundation and Channels, Retail Core Banking and Architecture, and Global Products and Technology Services.
We enjoy a flexible way of working and a highly collaborative environment, where fair and constructive feedback is encouraged.
For us, impact isn't a perk. It's the driver of our work. We are guided and rewarded by a shared desire to make the world a better place, one innovative solution at a time. Our colleagues make it their job to do impactful things and they love doing it in good company. Do you?
Casyis an end‑to‑end banking service that enables customers to view and manage all their internal and external bank accounts in one place. The platform leverages the EuropeanPSD2 (Payment Services Directive 2)initiative to provide secure, compliant and seamless account aggregation and transaction management.
Verification of Payee (VoP)is a critical component of the platform, designed to prevent payment fraud by validating beneficiary details before payments are processed.
Understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions;
Work with ING standard frameworks, tools and processes;
Analyse, develop, test and deliver user stories according to ING standards and team best practices;
Keep technical and risk documentation up to date;
Provide support to consumers;
Share knowledge and collaborate with team members.
What you’ll bring to the team
Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and Romanian;
Team‑oriented mindset in an international environment;
Quality‑focused, service‑oriented and eager to learn;
Curiosity for the latest developments in technology and financial services;
Good understanding of banking concepts or strong motivation to learn;
Ability to collaborate with stakeholders and Product Owners and translate business needs into valuable software solutions;
Strong problem‑solving and analytical thinking;
Solid understanding of Software Architecture;
Experience with Continuous Delivery;
Openness to innovation and creative solutions in a dynamic environment.
Required technical skills:
Spring Framework & Spring Boot
REST APIs & Swagger / OpenAPI
SQL (e.g. Oracle, MS SQL)
Persistence frameworks (JPA, Hibernate)
Gatling (performance testing);
Cloud experience (Kubernetes / OpenShift);
Experience with DevOps practices;
Experience building applications from scratch.
University degree in Computer Science, Cybernetics or equivalent experience (3+ years);
Experience working inAgile environments;
Familiarity with CI/CD tools and principles: Git, Jenkins, Artifactory, Azure DevOps;
Strong delivery track record.
